/target
Cargo.lock.bak
**/*.rs.bk
*.swp
.DS_Store

# Test/playwright ephemeral artifacts
.meta-snapshots/
.playwright-mcp/

# Agent harness output (generated, not committed)
.agent/
.archive/

# envctl.lock IS committed — it is the content-hashed manifest-of-record and the
# baseline for `envctl lock --check` (the CI drift gate). Do not ignore it.

# .handoff is git-tracked TEXT in full — the complete continuity audit trail (backlog.md /
# loop_state.md / HANDOFF.md / cycle/ / _done/ AND the loop control sentinels DONE/NEEDS-HUMAN/
# STOP and run logs) is committed so a fresh session resumes cold with nothing left behind.
#
# ADR-0004 fail-safe (the ONE exception, CI-enforced by ci/gates/p7.sh §3c): the per-repo
# .handoff is TEXT ONLY — the witnessed binary ledger lives at $META_ROOT/.handoff/ledger.db,
# never here. Never commit a binary ledger into this repo.
.handoff/**/ledger.db
.handoff/**/ledger.db.*

# hf transport notices are regenerated from witnessed events; the committed packet/card layer is
# the durable handoff state.
.handoff/deliveries/

# Runtime claim locks are ephemeral coordination state, not durable handoff text.
.handoff/locks/
